1. Introduction
In this experiment, I learned how to build a Provider-Agnostic LLM Client using Python. The main objective was to understand how a single application can communicate with different Large Language Model (LLM) providers, such as Gemini and Ollama, without changing the entire application code.

2. What I Did
Created a Python-based LLM client application.
Explored different LLM providers, including Google Gemini and Ollama.
Implemented an LLM client using separate Python files.
Created llm_client.py to handle communication with LLM providers.
Created main.py to accept user input and display model responses.
Created test_client.py for testing the client.
Used Ollama with the locally downloaded Llama 3.2 model.
Executed the application and received responses from the local LLM.

