5. What I Understood
Provider-Agnostic Architecture: An application can support multiple LLM providers using a common client interface.
LLM Providers: Different services provide access to language models.
Ollama: Allows us to download and run language models locally.
Llama 3.2: A language model that generates responses to user prompts.
Client Implementation: A client manages communication between the Python application and the selected LLM provider.
Modular Programming: Dividing an application into separate files makes the code easier to understand, maintain, and test.

6.What I Learned
How to build a basic LLM client using Python.
How different LLM providers can be integrated into one application.
